OL,3,GNEWSACoastal area to lose all-weather
OL,4,Alifeboat
OL,5,
OL,6,FPort St Mary's all-weather lifeboat
OL,7,Fwill be retired in 2028 and will not be
OL,8,Freplaced, the RNLI has confirmed.
OL,10,FThe station will instead rely on a
OL,11,Fsmaller D-class inshore lifeboat, with
OL,12,Fsupport from other lifeboat stations on
OL,13,Fthe Isle of Man.
OL,15,FMeanwhile, Douglas will receive one of
OL,16,Fthe charity's new coastal lifeboats,
OL,17,Fwhich are due to enter service from
OL,18,F2028.
OL,20,FThe RNLI said the changes reflected how
OL,21,Fthe sea was now used, with most rescues
OL,22,Ftaking place close to shore.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
